# Node starts runtime threads at startup (the V8 Inspector agent via
# node::inspector::Agent::Start -> pthread_create, plus libuv threadpool workers).
# glibc allocates each thread's TLS/DTV with calloc, and valgrind reports the block
# as "possibly lost" because only interior pointers reach it. It is a Node runtime
# artifact, not an lksctp allocation (lksctp is single-threaded and never calls
# pthread_create), and it shows up for every Node process.
#
# The frames between pthread_create and node::Start drift across Node versions (an
# added StartDebugSignalHandler frame, a delegating CreateEnvironment overload, a
# StartInternal frame, ...), which is why this file previously needed one pinned
# block per build. Anchor instead on the new-thread TLS prefix and node::Start, and
# let "..." absorb the version-specific middle so this stays correct across upgrades.
{
   Node startup-thread TLS (version-robust)
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   fun:calloc
   fun:allocate_dtv
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   fun:allocate_stack
   fun:pthread_create@@GLIBC_2.34
   ...
   fun:_ZN4node5StartEiPPc
   fun:(below main)
}
